        "mission_intent": "Subject: Corrective Action Plan Tracking and Closure Process for FY24 Material Weaknesses\n\nTeam, we need to stand up a comprehensive corrective action plan tracking process for the three material weaknesses identified in our FY24 assurance statement, fully aligned with A-123 requirements. For each weakness, I need the responsible program offices to develop detailed remediation plans with critical path milestones leading to a firm correction date, and I want all three resolved and validated before the mid-year Senior Management Council review in March. At the same time, I need the process to ensure that no weakness is marked as corrected until the Senior Accountable Official has made a written determination supported by appropriate documentation confirming that sufficient corrective actions have been taken and independently validated through internal control testing \u2014 so please build in time for that testing cycle. Additionally, ensure we maintain accurate, continuously updated status records for each deficiency throughout the lifecycle, that all corrective actions are consistent with applicable laws, regulations, and agency policy, and that we incorporate resolution effectiveness into the performance appraisals of accountable managers. Any weaknesses that remain uncorrected at year-end must be fully disclosed with material items highlighted. I recognize the March timeline is aggressive given the validation requirements, but I need the team to commit to delivering on both the speed and the rigor \u2014 use best efforts to balance these priorities.",
